      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-04T14:16:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why is that not good?\n\nI\u0027ve set this up to impact on the Bazel build, which we know will run from where the executable is. It\u0027s a bit awkward to move executables and files around in Bazel-land, so I\u0027d like to understand why changing the behavior is bad.",
      "parentUuid": "5a9bb122_50f2c686",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 41,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 41,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "d1d291d46a397d2fade718eef80a97bdc47b7c85",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "477cb84a_e0e7728f",
        "filename": "bazel/BUILD.bazel",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 41,
      "author": {
        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-04T14:17:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This prevents skslc from being used unless you mimic the structure of a Skia checkout. It\u0027s intended to be a standalone utility that can exist on its own.",
      "parentUuid": "0bd1ed1b_d55737db",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 41,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 41,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "d1d291d46a397d2fade718eef80a97bdc47b7c85",
